WEBVTT

00:11.870 --> 00:14.886
I loved cute, pretty things.

00:15.747 --> 00:21.175
But I stopped saying so out loud
at some point. I don't remember when.

00:22.390 --> 00:26.744
All so I could live in the normal
world, when I was anything but.

02:04.572 --> 02:08.806
Th-Th-Thi-Th-This isn't a d-d-d-date, got it?!

02:08.996 --> 02:11.513
My, did you want it to be just the two of us?

02:12.504 --> 02:16.424
I'm surprised you even know
what a date is, Sakura.

02:16.461 --> 02:17.778
That's not…!

02:17.780 --> 02:21.169
By the way, Tsubaki, where are we going?

02:21.458 --> 02:25.606
Oh! I'm so sorry. I didn't explain a thing, did I?

02:26.806 --> 02:29.993
We're going to visit an old man named Ito.

02:30.700 --> 02:35.230
He lost his wife last year, and the
shock made him coop himself up.

02:35.538 --> 02:37.840
I pay him regular visits out of concern.

02:38.449 --> 02:40.264
And do you always bring those two?

02:40.400 --> 02:44.929
Mhm! But sometimes I bring
new kids to keep things fresh.

02:45.181 --> 02:47.827
Th-That sounds like a big responsibility.

02:47.975 --> 02:50.387
What, specifically, should we do?

02:50.873 --> 02:52.633
It's not that big a deal.

02:52.960 --> 02:56.701
Talk with him, help with the housework,
just be there for him.

02:57.390 --> 02:59.532
Share the power of youth with him!

03:00.375 --> 03:02.578
Welcome back, Tsubaki!

03:02.910 --> 03:07.021
I got some dorayaki from Nazuna
today. Let's eat them together!

03:07.126 --> 03:09.796
Eeee, I'm so happy! I love their dorayaki!

03:09.975 --> 03:11.476
Huh?! He's so cheery!

03:11.827 --> 03:13.680
How is this grieving?

03:13.753 --> 03:15.532
He's so cheery he glows.

03:15.636 --> 03:19.698
The yard's well-maintained, too.
I can't imagine he's depressed.

03:20.123 --> 03:23.575
Oh? I don't believe I've met these three.

03:23.673 --> 03:24.418
That's right.

03:24.787 --> 03:26.067
They're all first-years.

03:26.326 --> 03:27.735
N-Nice to meet you!

03:27.858 --> 03:28.640
Hello.

03:29.070 --> 03:33.101
Oh, I see! You Furin kids are all so stylish.

03:33.446 --> 03:36.523
Your hair is a lovely mimosa color.

03:36.584 --> 03:37.323
Mimosa?

03:37.538 --> 03:38.836
It's a type of flower.

03:39.126 --> 03:41.624
And your earring is coral, I see.

03:41.796 --> 03:45.224
It appears to be an antique,
but it suits you well!

03:45.938 --> 03:47.667
Oh, and you…

03:48.147 --> 03:49.686
Your eye is…

03:50.627 --> 03:53.206
a lovely dusk hue.

03:54.400 --> 03:57.624
It reminds me of a seaside trip
I took with the wife.

03:57.753 --> 03:59.618
Ah! I love that story!

04:00.116 --> 04:04.270
He says they stood together on
the beach until the sun fully set!

04:04.467 --> 04:06.116
So romantic!

04:06.424 --> 04:12.270
It was just so beautiful, we were rooted
to the spot until well after sunset.

04:12.756 --> 04:14.787
We stumbled the whole way home!

04:15.003 --> 04:17.076
What a sandy mess we were.

04:17.815 --> 04:21.600
Oh, my apologies! How rude of me,
to keep you standing here!

04:22.086 --> 04:23.249
Please, come in.

04:23.643 --> 04:24.923
Thank you.

04:25.698 --> 04:27.156
Huh? Sakura?

04:27.809 --> 04:29.643
Why is your face so red?

04:29.864 --> 04:30.707
Like I know!

04:32.609 --> 04:33.255
Oh?

04:33.993 --> 04:37.630
Gramps, you know you need to
put your leftovers in the fridge!

04:37.926 --> 04:39.876
Whoopsie! I totally forgot!

04:40.178 --> 04:43.495
And the light's burnt out, too.

04:43.612 --> 04:46.492
Ah, I was thinking of changing it!

04:46.781 --> 04:48.221
I can change it for you!

04:48.523 --> 04:50.073
Wow, really?

04:50.190 --> 04:52.584
Were you getting these ready for recycling?

04:52.732 --> 04:56.196
That's right! I went to the bathroom
and forgot all about it.

05:08.227 --> 05:10.166
Could you hold this?

05:10.406 --> 05:12.443
I'm going to go make some tea.

05:13.827 --> 05:15.550
Wait in the room in back.

05:16.504 --> 05:17.507
Okay…

05:18.695 --> 05:21.698
He said in back, so, back there?

05:33.938 --> 05:35.907
That's a lot of clothes.

05:36.621 --> 05:39.772
Enough to wear a different set
every day for a year.

05:40.160 --> 05:42.578
Oh, so sorry! I meant over here.

05:45.046 --> 05:47.021
It was so dusty in there.

05:47.852 --> 05:49.852
Nobody's wearing those anymore.

05:52.461 --> 05:53.815
Oh, right! Gramps.

05:55.076 --> 05:56.769
Let's go on a date sometime.

05:57.150 --> 05:57.803
Hm?

05:58.276 --> 06:02.566
It's gotten warmer, so we could dress up
and hit a cafe or theater!

06:02.930 --> 06:07.273
How about you wear that gray hat?
Like for the cherry blossoms two years ago!

06:07.716 --> 06:12.276
You two looked incredible back then!
Like a scene straight out of a movie!

06:12.793 --> 06:15.206
You and your wife liked to dress up, did you?

06:15.372 --> 06:16.646
That's wonderful.

06:17.107 --> 06:19.021
That explains all the clothes.

06:19.335 --> 06:21.316
She was always so stylish.

06:21.649 --> 06:26.892
In trying to understand her and get
her attention, I got hooked, myself!

06:27.243 --> 06:29.809
I gave her a nice one-piece at first,

06:30.123 --> 06:33.187
and it had such a loud floral pattern on it.

06:33.433 --> 06:35.673
Looking back, I can't believe she wore it,

06:36.172 --> 06:41.538
but she always wore the right shoes
and accessories to really pull it off.

06:42.160 --> 06:46.098
I love that story, too! She kept wearing it
for a long time, didn't she?

06:46.486 --> 06:48.658
She must have loved it!

06:50.295 --> 06:52.307
I certainly hope she did.

06:52.695 --> 06:55.347
What? Of course she did!

06:56.800 --> 07:00.098
She always smiled, but she was a quiet person.

07:00.375 --> 07:02.812
Never really talked a whole lot.

07:03.809 --> 07:04.929
But even so,

07:05.280 --> 07:08.609
the time we spent together was always so happy.

07:09.384 --> 07:11.680
For me, at least.

07:12.492 --> 07:14.904
It sounds like a beautiful relationship.

07:18.098 --> 07:19.396
Thanks for having us.

07:19.600 --> 07:20.652
I'll be back.

07:20.978 --> 07:21.538
Mhm!

07:22.535 --> 07:24.418
It's all thanks to seeing your eye.

07:24.775 --> 07:28.486
It brought back so many memories
of my wife. I had a great time!

07:29.033 --> 07:30.215
Thank you.

07:30.898 --> 07:32.596
I didn't do anything.

07:35.876 --> 07:38.443
I was worried when you said he was depressed,

07:38.609 --> 07:40.301
but he was surprisingly cheery!

07:40.781 --> 07:43.661
Well, he's certainly doing better than last year,

07:44.049 --> 07:47.778
but he still has times where
he looks like he's suffering.

07:48.264 --> 07:51.593
It's only natural, given he
lost someone so precious,

07:52.006 --> 07:54.824
but I think there's more to it than that.

07:56.080 --> 07:59.187
Of course, he'll just say
there isn't if you ask him!

08:02.547 --> 08:06.283
But still, I want him to get his vigor back.

08:07.120 --> 08:10.756
I'll do anything to help him have a good time.

08:11.981 --> 08:13.415
Why are you so invested?

08:14.393 --> 08:18.049
Because I owe him and his wife a great deal.

08:21.612 --> 08:22.744
They loved me.

08:23.396 --> 08:24.929
As I am.

08:26.689 --> 08:28.633
Look at this! Isn't it cute?

08:28.713 --> 08:29.840
It really is!

08:29.870 --> 08:31.206
So cute!

08:31.876 --> 08:32.701
Thanks!

08:32.836 --> 08:35.600
Whatcha doin', Tsubakino? Let's go!

08:36.572 --> 08:37.366
'Kay.

08:38.258 --> 08:38.873
So cute!

08:40.221 --> 08:42.621
Ugh, those girls are at it again.

08:42.953 --> 08:46.492
They never say anything
but "cute". Who even cares?

08:46.756 --> 08:47.360
Right?

08:48.240 --> 08:49.883
Y-Yeah.

08:52.030 --> 08:53.027
Oh, right!

08:53.464 --> 08:54.381
Take this!

08:56.215 --> 08:58.683
You said you like these cars, didn't you?

09:00.473 --> 09:03.335
Th-Thanks! I love it.

09:03.464 --> 09:04.141
No prob!

09:04.664 --> 09:06.400
See ya tomorrow!

09:06.830 --> 09:09.187
If they had a motorcycle, I'd want that!

09:15.040 --> 09:16.972
S-So cute!

09:17.446 --> 09:20.720
Oh, wow! This one's a nice color,

09:20.873 --> 09:22.781
but I prefer this one's shape!

09:23.058 --> 09:24.904
When I get home, I'll put this…

09:38.116 --> 09:39.070
You liar.

09:44.916 --> 09:46.233
Did someone drop this?

09:47.833 --> 09:49.243
It's so pretty!

09:50.147 --> 09:50.935
Ahh!

09:51.181 --> 09:52.264
Sonny, that!

09:52.726 --> 09:53.870
That earring!

09:57.064 --> 10:00.812
That's my wife's! I've been
looking for it all day!

10:01.353 --> 10:04.984
My, thank you so much for finding it!

10:08.098 --> 10:11.292
He's a man, but his shirt is pink!

10:12.030 --> 10:16.240
I don't really know why, but he looks wonderful!

10:16.935 --> 10:18.787
Sonny, do you like dorayaki?

10:18.836 --> 10:19.310
Eh?

10:20.406 --> 10:23.058
Yui! Found your earring!

10:23.710 --> 10:25.778
A kid picked it up on his way by.

10:26.030 --> 10:27.618
My, is that so?

10:27.926 --> 10:29.821
He's waiting in the entrance now.

10:30.190 --> 10:32.295
Thought I'd send him home with dorayaki.

10:41.446 --> 10:44.467
Are you the one who found my earring for me?

10:44.923 --> 10:46.116
Thank you!

10:48.061 --> 10:48.627
Here you go! Pick your favorite.

10:48.630 --> 10:50.535
[Nazuna]
Here you go! Pick your favorite.

10:50.929 --> 10:54.443
Oh? What's wrong? Do you
not like dorayaki, after all?

10:54.578 --> 10:56.953
Ah, no, it's…

10:57.544 --> 10:58.750
It's, um…

10:59.643 --> 11:02.387
Ma'am, your clothes are so pretty.

11:03.569 --> 11:06.221
Aren't they? They're gorgeous!

11:06.516 --> 11:08.443
I requested this outfit.

11:08.553 --> 11:11.095
I thought it'd be perfect for the season.

11:11.421 --> 11:13.403
You know your fashion, don't you?

11:13.513 --> 11:15.101
N-No, I barely…

11:15.430 --> 11:20.596
My wife is always dressing up, so we'd
love if you came back to see more outfits.

11:25.587 --> 11:29.956
After that, I started visiting
them almost every day.

11:30.996 --> 11:31.840
Every time,

11:32.166 --> 11:35.440
I had a blast seeing them in
all their lovely clothes.

11:54.350 --> 11:55.636
What do you think?

11:55.796 --> 11:58.227
I-I'm a boy, so…

11:59.218 --> 12:00.560
I don't really know.

12:00.683 --> 12:04.400
Yui! Where do we keep our tea leaves, again?

12:06.209 --> 12:07.538
Coming.

12:20.787 --> 12:22.818
Want to try it, Tasuku?

12:23.292 --> 12:25.581
N-No! I was just…!

12:27.618 --> 12:29.341
It's perfectly okay.

12:32.356 --> 12:33.433
All done.

12:34.658 --> 12:36.356
Tea's on, you two.

12:36.855 --> 12:40.615
Tasuku! You put on lipstick? Looking good!

12:44.036 --> 12:45.323
T-Tasuku?

12:45.360 --> 12:46.061
Why…?

12:46.855 --> 12:49.636
Why does this make me happy?

12:50.676 --> 12:54.652
Normal boys don't put on lipstick
and get happy about it!

12:55.156 --> 12:59.747
So why do I think it's pretty and get happy?!

13:00.338 --> 13:04.412
I don't want to keep lying
to my friends and family!

13:05.021 --> 13:07.747
I want to like the same things as everyone else!

13:08.720 --> 13:11.120
I want to be normal!

13:15.390 --> 13:17.230
Hey, Tasuku.

13:18.972 --> 13:21.316
Do you know about high heels?

13:21.790 --> 13:22.664
Huh?

13:23.107 --> 13:26.621
You mean those women's shoes
with the pointy heels?

13:26.836 --> 13:28.824
Yes! But the thing is,

13:29.156 --> 13:31.501
they were originally for men.

13:34.098 --> 13:35.132
That's right!

13:35.323 --> 13:41.963
They were designed so men could keep
themselves stable using a bow on horseback!

13:43.489 --> 13:44.516
Really?

13:45.200 --> 13:49.600
And makeup was originally
a charm to keep you safe.

13:55.452 --> 13:58.916
The differences between men
and women are important,

13:59.353 --> 14:02.935
but it's no more than one part of who you are.

14:03.606 --> 14:04.227
Huh?

14:04.572 --> 14:09.470
After all, the first person to wear high heels,
and the first to wear lipstick?

14:09.741 --> 14:15.981
They didn't say "this is for men" or
"this is for women" beforehand.

14:16.369 --> 14:20.240
They only thought that they liked them,
and wanted to wear them.

14:21.046 --> 14:27.661
You asked why you were happy
even though you were a boy,

14:28.018 --> 14:29.760
but that's not quite it.

14:33.600 --> 14:36.449
You had those thoughts because you're you.

14:38.412 --> 14:41.858
Thoughts that a lot of people
share get called "normal",

14:42.350 --> 14:46.978
but that's a vague thing that changes with time,
just like high heels and makeup.

14:47.452 --> 14:52.270
So you can keep on liking the things
that make you happy, Tasuku.

14:54.920 --> 15:00.707
You like the things you do, no matter what
they are, and I love you just like that.

15:02.640 --> 15:06.713
Me, too! Me, too! I love you
just the way you are, Tasuku!

15:07.624 --> 15:09.003
And done.

15:09.193 --> 15:12.313
Man, I can see how this would make you happy!

15:12.584 --> 15:13.606
Right?

15:16.978 --> 15:19.698
After all, it suits you so well!

15:25.126 --> 15:27.009
I was afraid.

15:27.741 --> 15:30.092
Of being ostracized for being different.

15:31.009 --> 15:34.603
But those two accepted me as I was.

15:35.280 --> 15:36.713
Told me they loved me.

15:37.606 --> 15:39.476
I wasn't alone anymore.

15:40.332 --> 15:42.523
I could say I liked what I liked.

15:44.012 --> 15:45.735
So now it's my turn!

15:50.744 --> 15:52.387
A-Are you okay?!

15:53.033 --> 15:54.664
I was just so moved…

15:55.532 --> 15:58.196
Ito deserves to enjoy himself.

15:58.560 --> 16:00.849
We need to find out what's bothering him.

16:03.335 --> 16:04.886
So we'll help out!

16:05.452 --> 16:07.083
Right, Suo?

16:07.175 --> 16:08.116
Right you are.

16:08.264 --> 16:09.347
Sakura!

16:12.350 --> 16:13.452
When?

16:13.507 --> 16:14.129
Huh?

16:14.369 --> 16:17.107
The next visit. When is it?

16:19.833 --> 16:23.606
Eeee, you're all such good guys!
I love it! I love you!

16:23.926 --> 16:27.310
Let's strike while the iron's hot! Tomorrow it is!

16:27.396 --> 16:28.492
Tomorrow?!

16:29.427 --> 16:32.215
After talking about my wife with you yesterday,

16:32.529 --> 16:35.175
I felt compelled to dig out the old albums.

16:35.452 --> 16:38.516
I loved this old one-piece!

16:38.683 --> 16:40.830
The cloth fluttered as she walked,

16:41.046 --> 16:42.880
- which suited her perfectly.
- He's smitten.

16:43.390 --> 16:46.000
He really does seem cheery, though!

16:46.110 --> 16:49.003
At a glance, he seems unbothered.

16:49.329 --> 16:50.455
But these…

16:50.769 --> 16:52.510
They're all Granny!

16:52.830 --> 16:55.101
And she's hardly ever facing the camera.

16:55.630 --> 16:58.430
She always turned away from the camera.

16:58.824 --> 17:00.700
It felt more like I snuck shots!

17:00.700 --> 17:01.907
Is he a voyeur?

17:02.160 --> 17:05.390
Do you not have any pictures of the two of you?

17:05.790 --> 17:07.495
Like from your wedding?

17:07.716 --> 17:10.609
Oh! It's not from our wedding, but…

17:13.600 --> 17:14.541
Here.

17:14.898 --> 17:16.529
Huh? Is this your yard?

17:17.249 --> 17:18.141
It is!

17:22.615 --> 17:23.846
Oh! Are you alright?

17:23.850 --> 17:25.963
Was the picture really that surprising?

17:26.147 --> 17:29.550
Nire, I don't think Sakura was surprised.

17:29.698 --> 17:30.110
Eh?

17:30.393 --> 17:32.603
Oh, Sakura…

17:32.953 --> 17:35.987
Did seeing this make your romance sensor go off?

17:36.787 --> 17:39.649
Shut up! My castella just went
down the wrong pipe!

17:39.809 --> 17:40.400
Hm?

17:40.540 --> 17:43.600
Gramps, this boy can sense, uh, romantic auras?

17:43.821 --> 17:46.670
And when he does, he turns red!

17:46.738 --> 17:47.286
Bnghk!

17:47.316 --> 17:49.083
Oh, I see! I see.

17:49.156 --> 17:52.000
So, Sakura, how did this photo look to you?

17:52.166 --> 17:55.292
H-How? It's just…

17:55.969 --> 17:56.652
H…

17:56.996 --> 18:01.532
Happy…? Fun…?

18:01.920 --> 18:04.240
Uuugh, you know.

18:04.695 --> 18:07.409
She looked like Tsubaki,

18:07.735 --> 18:10.400
wh-when he was talking to Umemiya.

18:14.610 --> 18:18.627
G-Gosh! I looked that cute?! Oh, you!

18:18.812 --> 18:20.301
Wow, he's beet red!

18:20.344 --> 18:21.169
Nicely done.

18:21.427 --> 18:22.732
Wow, so embarrassing!

18:23.064 --> 18:26.024
Oh, Gramps, Umemiya is, well,

18:26.100 --> 18:28.406
a guy I talk to all the time, and who I lo…

18:33.083 --> 18:35.280
G-Gramps, what's wrong?!

18:39.138 --> 18:41.581
Does it really… look like that to you?

18:42.516 --> 18:43.889
Why do you ask?

18:45.243 --> 18:47.987
I've been worried ever since she left.

18:48.818 --> 18:51.784
About whether Yui was actually happy.

18:52.221 --> 18:53.003
Huh?

18:53.360 --> 18:57.353
I loved her, and was over the moon, but…

18:58.221 --> 18:59.766
It was an arranged marriage.

19:00.153 --> 19:03.932
And Yui was never the type to speak her mind.

19:04.824 --> 19:07.704
I wondered how she felt about it.

19:08.430 --> 19:13.193
I get it. So this is what Tsubaki felt.
What was bothering him.

19:13.766 --> 19:14.923
Why would you…

19:15.144 --> 19:18.843
When she was still here,
it never really bothered me,

19:19.483 --> 19:23.433
but now that I'm alone,
that anxiety has only grown.

19:24.276 --> 19:24.880
But…

19:25.772 --> 19:28.633
I see. That's how you see it.

19:29.944 --> 19:31.532
That's a bit of a relief.

19:33.390 --> 19:36.055
Excuse me, may I ask a question?

19:36.196 --> 19:36.726
Hm?

19:37.298 --> 19:39.895
What kind of picture is that?

19:40.073 --> 19:40.510
Eh?

19:40.880 --> 19:43.563
I've been curious since our visit yesterday,

19:43.895 --> 19:47.052
but the garden is full of non-flowering trees,

19:47.366 --> 19:49.476
so the flowering dogwood jumped out.

19:49.480 --> 19:50.295
Trees jump?

19:50.356 --> 19:52.240
And you took this in front of it…

19:52.603 --> 19:54.892
Ohh, good eye.

19:55.181 --> 19:57.618
Tending the garden was my personal hobby,

19:57.901 --> 20:01.618
but Yui suddenly suggested
planting a flowering dogwood.

20:02.300 --> 20:07.686
She was usually against it, but after we
planted it, she asked for a photo together.

20:08.523 --> 20:13.310
Sir, did anything happen before you planted it?

20:13.612 --> 20:14.203
Eh?

20:14.535 --> 20:16.701
Anything, no matter how trivial.

20:17.360 --> 20:18.633
Hmm…

20:19.446 --> 20:21.372
Ah! If I had to guess…

20:21.913 --> 20:23.218
Yui, Yui!

20:23.310 --> 20:24.430
On our next holiday…

20:24.535 --> 20:27.304
Oh! Did something happen?

20:27.710 --> 20:28.455
Ah…

20:29.378 --> 20:33.686
Oh, no. I just wanted to clip my
nails somewhere brighter.

20:33.883 --> 20:35.095
You can keep working.

20:46.867 --> 20:50.036
You're always so lovely when
you're absorbed in fashion.

20:50.812 --> 20:55.790
I want to be fashionable enough
to make you look at me that way.

20:56.381 --> 20:58.929
You always say I'm lovely,

20:59.323 --> 21:01.040
but never look at me…

21:01.692 --> 21:04.387
You don't face me, look sulky,

21:04.892 --> 21:07.101
and get embarrassed afterward.

21:07.747 --> 21:11.907
Now that I think about it, I might
have been worried back then, too.

21:12.972 --> 21:15.624
Well, she never said anything then, either.

21:16.233 --> 21:19.175
Maybe the tree was just another of her whims.

21:19.729 --> 21:21.766
It's too late to find out now.

21:22.375 --> 21:24.387
- I wish I had asked her more.

21:24.387 --> 21:24.966
- No.
- I wish I had asked her more.

21:25.446 --> 21:28.024
She seems to have been angry at you.

21:29.236 --> 21:30.018
Huh?

21:30.369 --> 21:32.221
Wh-What do you mean?

21:35.360 --> 21:38.738
Flowering dogwoods represent persistence,

21:39.280 --> 21:40.516
and vibrant romance.

21:41.372 --> 21:42.135
It asks,

21:42.812 --> 21:44.923
"Am I indifferent to you?"

21:45.932 --> 21:48.221
"Do you think I don't love you?"

21:52.867 --> 21:58.203
That flowering dogwood is a
slightly spiteful refutation.

22:00.984 --> 22:02.424
You didn't get it at all.

22:03.667 --> 22:06.880
Gramps, you didn't understand her!

22:08.203 --> 22:11.698
She's the one who taught me
it was okay to like what I like!

22:13.095 --> 22:15.913
She wouldn't stay with someone she didn't love!

22:16.670 --> 22:18.055
Tsubaki…

22:18.572 --> 22:19.384
I agree.

22:19.790 --> 22:24.172
If I had someone who spoke about
me so passionately at my side,

22:25.243 --> 22:26.252
I just know,

22:27.384 --> 22:28.572
it'd make me happy.

22:32.030 --> 22:33.403
Isn't that right, Sakura?

22:33.470 --> 22:34.707
Huh? M-Me?!

22:36.055 --> 22:38.732
I don't really know, but…

22:39.846 --> 22:43.815
Someone who doesn't care wouldn't make that face.

22:47.070 --> 22:49.046
I suppose… you're right.

22:49.766 --> 22:52.209
Yui wasn't that sort of person.

22:52.738 --> 22:55.341
Here I was, closer to her than anyone, and yet…

22:56.270 --> 22:58.566
What a fool I was.

23:00.326 --> 23:02.221
Thank you, boys.

23:04.603 --> 23:06.695
And Yui, I'm sorry.

23:07.532 --> 23:09.815
But even if I was in the wrong,

23:10.024 --> 23:11.520
this was a refutation?

23:12.258 --> 23:15.021
I doubt you ever intended for me to find out.

23:15.920 --> 23:18.898
You always were stylish. Always.

23:20.406 --> 23:21.550
Really…

23:22.953 --> 23:24.640
I could never match up.

23:26.968 --> 23:29.971
[Unspoken Feelings]

23:30.400 --> 23:33.618
Sakura, your blush radar sure is finely-tuned!

23:33.723 --> 23:34.873
Blush radar?

23:34.923 --> 23:38.055
You know, how you sense
feelings of love and turn red!

23:38.116 --> 23:40.584
I-I-I-It's not like that!

23:40.646 --> 23:43.489
Oh? Then could I get you to look that way?

23:43.556 --> 23:45.950
Huh? There's nobody over there.

23:46.166 --> 23:47.501
Don't worry about it.

23:47.840 --> 23:49.821
Ah! A lovey-dovey couple!

23:50.584 --> 23:51.741
Oh, and look there!

23:51.858 --> 23:54.824
Some preschoolers are walking hand-in-hand!

23:56.510 --> 23:57.750
Oh, and now there's…

23:57.750 --> 23:59.458
Stop playing with me!
